# OpenTUI skill is required

Before implementing, reviewing, or debugging **anything** in this repo — and
**especially** terminal UI (`src/cli.tsx`, `src/app.tsx`, `src/pages/`,
`src/components/`, `scripts/smoke.tsx`) — read and follow the OpenTUI skill at
`~/.agents/skills/opentui/SKILL.md`. Then open the skill docs it points at for
the task (React bindings, layout, keyboard, testing, components).

Do not guess OpenTUI APIs from Ink habits or from prior session memory. Check
the skill first: lowercase intrinsics (`<box>`, `<text>`, `<input>`,
`<select>`), default colours (`#FFFFFF` text/cursor, dark select fills),
`flexShrink` / Yoga overflow, `useKeyboard`, `testRender`.

YACOW is `@opentui/core` + `@opentui/react` on Bun 1.3+ (decision 2.1). QR
codes stay on the `qrcode` package (decision 6.10), not `@opentui/qrcode`.
Theme-aware text uses `FG` / `MUTED` / `ACCENT` (decision 6.12); never a bare
`<input>` — use `TextInput`.
